{"id": "EUVD-2026-25472", "enisaUuid": "59c00de6-5067-383b-bf8e-447de6d4fea6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwireguard: device: use exit_rtnl callback instead of manual rtnl_lock in pre_exit\n\nwg_netns_pre_exit() manually acquires rtnl_lock() inside the\npernet .pre_exit callback.  This causes a hung task when another\nthread holds rtnl_mutex - the cleanup_net workqueue (or the\nsetup_net failure rollback path) blocks indefinitely in\nwg_netns_pre_exit() waiting to acquire the lock.\n\nConvert to .exit_rtnl, introduced in commit 7a60d91c690b (\"net:\nAdd ->exit_rtnl() hook to struct pernet_operations.\"), where the\nframework already holds RTNL and batches all callbacks under a\nsingle rtnl_lock()/rtnl_unlock() pair, eliminating the contention\nwindow.\n\nThe rcu_assign_pointer(wg->creating_net, NULL) is safe to move\nfrom .pre_exit to .exit_rtnl (which runs after synchronize_rcu())\nbecause all RCU readers of creating_net either use maybe_get_net()\n- which returns NULL for a dying namespace with zero refcount - or\naccess net->user_ns which remains valid throughout the entire\nops_undo_list sequence.\n\n[ Jason: added __net_exit and __read_mostly annotations that were missing. ]", "datePublished": "2026-04-24T14:42:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/707607db2193591b68c0e70f814133472c185b1e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a9e69155b2091b8297afaf1533b8d68a3096841", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c52ef00e391144334f10995985c2f256d4be982", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1d0f6cbb962af29586e3e65a4bced1a5e39221f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60a25ef8dacb3566b1a8c4de00572a498e2a3bf9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-31579", "GHSA-h53c-6597-vmfw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c89bae7-5dfc-32bd-8a8d-9aabd31a1620", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.24"}, {"id": "2afe8393-1a34-3e35-9d56-6022c4bd96fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "900575aa33a3eaaef802b31de187a85c4a4b4bd0 <707607db2193591b68c0e70f814133472c185b1e"}, {"id": "4540145d-cd1d-3a2c-bb1d-824957345869", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "900575aa33a3eaaef802b31de187a85c4a4b4bd0 <1c52ef00e391144334f10995985c2f256d4be982"}, {"id": "5112ea8d-759d-3b6b-bd03-b097e2e685de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "900575aa33a3eaaef802b31de187a85c4a4b4bd0 <60a25ef8dacb3566b1a8c4de00572a498e2a3bf9"}, {"id": "78b075ed-7183-30ec-9e3d-df86439cfa7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "900575aa33a3eaaef802b31de187a85c4a4b4bd0 <a1d0f6cbb962af29586e3e65a4bced1a5e39221f"}, {"id": "8a4268a0-8860-30fd-8dbb-db54ef66be0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "976380f9-e100-33c2-bbe1-2fd642f6928a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "900575aa33a3eaaef802b31de187a85c4a4b4bd0 <9a9e69155b2091b8297afaf1533b8d68a3096841"}, {"id": "b73cc807-7ce8-311f-950b-18accdacb1bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "bb59a8d7-90bf-3e4b-889a-85e2f7137e42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "d81d7985-fd46-30ce-b99b-f333e95f154d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7.7 <5.8"}, {"id": "db99f35c-f1b0-3d2f-b8b9-3a542842999d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "363cc6efdbb54bb06cd5034a69b41aae974a736f"}, {"id": "fa33a385-2c33-3faf-a416-ae78e3b6b590", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.1"}, {"id": "fd0cb206-3224-3c26-8b11-6f96c6331101", "product": {"n